      "notes": "<h2>Advanced Cell Biology</h2>\n<p>This section explains advanced cellular processes including cell division stages, cancer biology, stem cells, and membrane transport mechanisms.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3> 1. MITOSIS (CELL DIVISION IN DETAIL)</h3>\n<p>Mitosis produces two identical daughter cells.</p>\n<pre>\nProphase → Metaphase → Anaphase → Telophase → Cytokinesis\n</pre>\n<h4> Prophase</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Chromosomes become visible</li>\n<li>Nuclear membrane breaks down</li>\n</ul>\n<h4> Metaphase</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Chromosomes align at equator</li>\n</ul>\n<h4> Anaphase</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Chromatids pulled to opposite poles</li>\n</ul>\n<h4> Telophase</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Nuclear membranes reform</li>\n<li>Two nuclei form</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3> 2. CANCER (UNCONTROLLED MITOSIS)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Cells divide uncontrollably</li>\n<li>Forms tumors</li>\n<li>Caused by mutations</li>\n</ul>\n<h4> Causes:</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Radiation</li>\n<li>Chemicals</li>\n<li>Genetic factors</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3> 3. STEM CELLS</h3>\n<p>Undifferentiated cells that can become different cell types.</p>\n<h4> Uses:</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Repair damaged tissues</li>\n<li>Treatment of diseases</li>\n<li>Regenerative medicine</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3> 4. DIFFERENTIATION vs SPECIALIZATION</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Differentiation:</b> process of cells becoming different types</li>\n<li><b>Specialization:</b> cells adapted for specific functions</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3> 5. CELL TRANSPORT MECHANISMS</h3>\n<h4> Endocytosis</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Cell takes in materials</li>\n<li>Membrane surrounds substance</li>\n</ul>\n<h4> Exocytosis</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Cell releases materials</li>\n<li>Vesicles fuse with membrane</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3> REAL EXAMPLES</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Cancer:</b> uncontrolled cell division forms tumors in organs.</li>\n<li><b>Stem cells:</b> used to repair damaged skin or blood cells.</li>\n<li><b>Endocytosis:</b> white blood cells engulf bacteria.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3> SUMMARY</h3>\n<pre>\nMitosis → Growth & repair\nCancer → uncontrolled division\nStem cells → repair system\nTransport → cell intake & output\n</pre>\n",
