      "notes": "<h2>Reproduction (Sexual vs Asexual)</h2>\n<p>This phase is designed to help you master exam questions by clearly understanding how sexual and asexual reproduction differ and when to use each concept in answers.</p>\n\n<hr>\n\n<h3> 1. SEXUAL VS ASEXUAL REPRODUCTION (DEEP COMPARISON)</h3>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\">\n  <tr>\n    <th>Feature</th>\n    <th>Asexual Reproduction</th>\n    <th>Sexual Reproduction</th>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>Number of parents</td>\n    <td>One parent</td>\n    <td>Two parents (male & female)</td>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>Gametes involved</td>\n    <td>None</td>\n    <td>Sperm and egg</td>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>Fertilization</td>\n    <td>Not involved</td>\n    <td>Occurs</td>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>Genetic variation</td>\n    <td>No variation (identical offspring)</td>\n    <td>High variation (different offspring)</td>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>Speed</td>\n    <td>Very fast</td>\n    <td>Slower process</td>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>Complexity</td>\n    <td>Simple</td>\n    <td>Complex</td>\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n    <td>Examples</td>\n    <td>Bacteria, Amoeba, yeast, potato</td>\n    <td>Humans, animals, flowering plants</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n<hr>\n\n<h3> 2. KEY SIMILARITIES</h3>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Both produce new individuals</li>\n  <li>Both ensure continuation of species</li>\n  <li>Both involve cell division</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n\n<h3> 3. EXAM-LEVEL UNDERSTANDING (IMPORTANT IDEAS)</h3>\n\n<h4> Asexual reproduction is best for:</h4>\n<ul>\n  <li>Rapid population increase</li>\n  <li>Stable environments</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4> Sexual reproduction is best for:</h4>\n<ul>\n  <li>Changing environments</li>\n  <li>Survival through variation</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n\n<h3> 4. COMMON EXAM MISTAKES</h3>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Saying asexual reproduction has fertilization (WRONG)</li>\n  <li>Confusing zygote with embryo</li>\n  <li>Mixing gametes in asexual reproduction</li>\n  <li>Thinking variation happens in asexual reproduction</li>\n</ul>\n<h3> 6. QUICK REVISION SUMMARY</h3>\n\n<pre>\nASEXUAL:\n- 1 parent\n- No gametes\n- No fertilization\n- Identical offspring\n- Fast reproduction\n\nSEXUAL:\n- 2 parents\n- Gametes involved\n- Fertilization occurs\n- Variation produced\n- Slower reproduction\n</pre>\n<hr>\n<h3> 7. MASTER KEY IDEA</h3>\n\n<p><b>Asexual reproduction = speed & survival in stable conditions</b></p>\n<p><b>Sexual reproduction = variation & survival in changing conditions</b></p>\n",
